      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The East Line and Red River Railroad ran through Como in the late 1870s, and the town was renamed Carrollton in 1879.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/como-tx",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Lignite coal was discovered on J. Smith’s property by 1900, making it one of Como’s leading industries.",
